            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous bailout therapy of a perforated vein graft using a stent-autologous vein patch.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 74-yr-old man with two prior coronary bypass surgeries experienced perforation of an occluded aortocoronary vein graft during a transluminal extraction catheter (TEC) procedure for unstable angina. The perforation was successfully closed using a Palmaz 154 stent covered with a short segment of autologous antecubital vein.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
